.TH "CSDLC-REMOTE" "1" "September 11, 2026" "C-SDLC v3" "ADL Operator Manual"
.SH NAME
csdlc\-remote \- list remote command routes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&csdlc remote \-\-help
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&Read\-only overview of github, github\-issue, github\-pr, pr\-state, publish and review. No request is accepted; invocation with no arguments also prints help. See each command page for its actual mutation boundary.
.SH OPTIONS
\&\-\-help: Show standalone help; \-h is equivalent.
.PP
\&\-h: Show standalone help; do not combine with execution options.
.SH REQUEST
\&No JSON request.
.SH EFFECTS
\&Observation or static model only. Read findings/status, not just process exit status; no release or lifecycle activation authority is granted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
\&csdlc remote \-\-help
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\&csdlc(1), csdlc\-requests(1).
